# File: big-remote-play/usr/share/big-remote-play/main.py, line: 58
#: src/big_remote_play/app.py:98
msgid ""
"The Story Behind the Project\n"
"\n"
"Big Remote Play was born from a real story of friendship, determination, and "
"the passion for Free Software.\n"
"\n"
"Alessandro e Silva Xavier (known as Alessandro) and Alexasandro Pacheco "
"Feliciano (known as Pacheco) wanted to play games together on BigLinux using "
"a feature that only existed on proprietary platforms like Steam Remote Play "
"and GeForce NOW. The problem? These systems are proprietary, locked to their "
"own ecosystems. If a game wasn't available on their platform, it was nearly "
"impossible to play remotely with friends.\n"
"\n"
"Refusing to accept this limitation, Alessandro and Pacheco embarked on a "
"journey of countless attempts and extensive research. After trying many "
"different approaches, they finally found a working solution by combining "
"multiple free software programs — including Sunshine, Moonlight, scripts, "
"and VPN tools. They had achieved what the proprietary platforms kept locked "
"behind their walls, and the best part: it was Free Software and multi-"
"platform!\n"
"\n"
"Excited by their success, they started sharing their achievement during "
"their live streams, which generated tremendous enthusiasm from the "
"community. However, there was a catch — the setup was complicated. It "
"required configuring multiple separate solutions: Sunshine, Moonlight, "
"custom scripts, VPN connections... it was a lot for anyone to handle.\n"
"\n"
"That's when a friend decided to step in and help develop a unified "
"application to simplify the entire process. And so, Big Remote Play was "
"born! 🎉\n"
"\n"
"An all-in-one application that integrates everything you need for remote "
"cooperative gaming — no proprietary platforms, no restrictions, no limits on "
"which games you can play."
msgstr ""
"La historia detrás del proyecto\n"
"\n"
"Big Remote Play nació de una historia real de amistad, determinación y la "
"pasión por el software libre.\n"
"\n"
"Alessandro e Silva Xavier (conocido como Alessandro) y Alexasandro Pacheco "
"Feliciano (conocido como Pacheco) querían jugar juntos en BigLinux "
"utilizando una función que solo existía en plataformas propietarias como "
"Steam Remote Play y GeForce NOW. ¿El problema? Estos sistemas son "
"propietarios, bloqueados en sus propios ecosistemas. Si un juego no estaba "
"disponible en su plataforma, era casi imposible jugar de forma remota con "
"amigos.\n"
"\n"
"Negándose a aceptar esta limitación, Alessandro y Pacheco se embarcaron en "
"un viaje de innumerables intentos e investigación extensa. Después de probar "
"muchos enfoques diferentes, finalmente encontraron una solución funcional "
"combinando múltiples programas de software libre, incluidos Sunshine, "
"Moonlight, scripts y herramientas VPN. Habían logrado lo que las plataformas "
"propietarias mantenían bloqueado tras sus muros, y la mejor parte: ¡era "
"software libre y multiplataforma!\n"
"\n"
"Emocionados por su éxito, comenzaron a compartir su logro durante sus "
"transmisiones en vivo, lo que generó un enorme entusiasmo en la comunidad. "
"Sin embargo, había un inconveniente: la configuración era complicada. "
"Requería configurar múltiples soluciones separadas: Sunshine, Moonlight, "
"scripts personalizados, conexiones VPN... era mucho para que cualquiera lo "
"manejara.\n"
"\n"
"Fue entonces cuando un amigo decidió intervenir y ayudar a desarrollar una "
"aplicación unificada para simplificar todo el proceso. ¡Y así nació Big "
"Remote Play! 🎉\n"
"\n"
"Una aplicación todo en uno que integra todo lo que necesitas para el juego "
"cooperativo remoto: sin plataformas propietarias, sin restricciones, sin "
"límites en los juegos que puedes jugar."

